From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandr Astrouski <astrouski@google.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: use link BSSID in MLO authentication replies

In send_auth_reply() for an MLD AP, sa is set to hapd->mld->mld_addr.
Setting reply->bssid to sa causes the authentication frame to carry
the MLD MAC address in Address 3 (BSSID) instead of the affiliated
AP link BSSID (hapd->own_addr).

Set reply->bssid to hapd->own_addr so the BSSID matches the transmitting
link AP.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Alexandr Astrouski <astrouski@google.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -455,3 +455,3 @@ static int send_auth_reply(struct hostap
 	os_memcpy(reply->sa, sa, ETH_ALEN);
-	os_memcpy(reply->bssid, sa, ETH_ALEN);
+	os_memcpy(reply->bssid, hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 
